Subject: [PATCH] dirnames: keep the instances in $LIMA_INSTANCES_DIR/<name>/lima

A program that embeds Lima keeps its own files for each instance (its
settings, markers, staged files). With every instance at $LIMA_HOME/<name>
they sit in another folder, and deleting an instance has to remove them
apart, so that one can outlive its instance.

When $LIMA_INSTANCES_DIR is set, the instance <name> is kept in
$LIMA_INSTANCES_DIR/<name>/lima, and the program owns the rest of
$LIMA_INSTANCES_DIR/<name>. $LIMA_HOME keeps what is shared (_config,
_networks, _disks, _templates). Unset, nothing changes.

A $LIMA_HOME per instance would do the same, but every instance would
then be named by the same folder: the guest hostnames and the SSH aliases
come from the instance name, and the Windows drivers name their WSL2
distro and HCS system after it. Naming the home after the instance
instead puts its name twice in the path of every socket, which the
sockets' length limit cannot afford (104 characters on macOS).

- dirnames.InstanceDir returns the new path, and dirnames.InstanceName is
  the name of an instance dir: the name is no longer the dir's base.
  Templates' {{.Name}} read it.
- store.Instances lists the folders that hold an instance folder, and
  store.Validate follows.
- Clone makes the parent folder of the new instance.

Tests TestInstancesDir, TestInstancesDirRelative, TestInstancesDirUnset.

---
diff -ruN a/pkg/instance/clone.go b/pkg/instance/clone.go
--- a/pkg/instance/clone.go	2026-10-20 00:21:33.801616607 +0200
+++ b/pkg/instance/clone.go	2026-10-20 00:22:24.894177976 +0200
@@ -53,6 +53,10 @@
